  "created": "2023-03-22T17:42:04.425Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The five second timer for queuing Image/String Url Downloaders repeatedly stacks when using Play Mode Settings with Reload Domain disabled.\n\nBasically, if these settings (under Project Settings -> Editor) are enabled in Unity, and the user enters Play Mode with one Url downloader in the scene, it will load instantly. If they leave and re-enter Play Mode again, it will download after five seconds. If they do this again, it will load after ten seconds, and so on.\n\nIf they have multiple Url Downloaders in the scene, say three, it will wait fifteen seconds the second time and thirty seconds the third, and so on.\n\nThis queue is reset during any compiler reload, say you've changed a script or don't have these Play Mode settings. Since Graph does not cause a compiler reload, the issue is especially noticeable when doing rapid iteration.\n\nClientSim added support for these Play Mode settings over CyanEmu which didn't, and I believe most creators should be using it for the incredible time save it makes.",
